<div class="article-body">
    <Fragment set:html={`<h2>Starting From Zero</h2>

      <p>First-attempt hold times vary widely. A hold of a few seconds is a normal starting point. Some people cannot hang at all yet. That is not a sign of weakness. Grip endurance usually improves with regular practice.</p>

      <p>Your pace depends on bodyweight and starting strength. Three sessions a week of 5 to 10 minutes each is a common plan. This is common training practice, not a tested prescription. Read the <a href="/how-to-deadhang/">how to dead hang guide</a> for the basic movement pattern before starting.</p>

      <p>Regression exercises build the grip foundation needed for a full dead hang. Start with these if you cannot hold the bar for 5 seconds yet.</p>

      <h2 id="cant-hang-yet">Can't Hang Yet? Start With This Ladder</h2>

      <p>If you cannot hang from the bar yet, start on the lowest rung and move up one rung at a time. Each rung removes a little support. The notes on when to move up are common training practice, not a tested prescription.</p>

      <div class="visual-block">
        <div class="dg-box"><div class="dg-box-head"><span>Starting ladder</span><span>Four rungs</span></div>
<ol class="sl-steps" aria-label="Starting ladder from a supported hang to Level 1">
<li><div class="sl-fig"><svg viewBox="0 0 120 140" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><rect x="1.5" y="1.5" width="117" height="137" rx="6" fill="#0e1420" stroke="#2a3a54" stroke-width="1.5"/><line x1="10" y1="128" x2="110" y2="128" stroke="#8090b0" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"/><g stroke="#00e5ff" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" fill="none"><line x1="60" y1="46" x2="60" y2="84"/><polyline points="50,44 42,58 40,58"/><polyline points="70,44 78,58 80,58"/><line x1="60" y1="84" x2="53" y2="126"/><line x1="60" y1="84" x2="67" y2="126"/></g><circle cx="60" cy="30" r="7" fill="#00e5ff"/><line x1="14" y1="58" x2="106" y2="58" stroke="#8090b0" stroke-width="5" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg></div><div class="sl-text"><p class="sl-name"><span class="sl-n">Rung 1</span> Supported hang</p><p><span class="sl-k">What it looks like</span>Feet flat on the floor or a box, hands on a low bar. Your legs carry most of your weight and the bar takes a small share.</p><p><span class="sl-k">Ready for the next rung when</span>You finish your planned sets with steady form and no pain, and shifting a little more weight onto the bar feels manageable.</p></div></li>
<li><div class="sl-fig"><svg viewBox="0 0 120 140" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><rect x="1.5" y="1.5" width="117" height="137" rx="6" fill="#0e1420" stroke="#2a3a54" stroke-width="1.5"/><line x1="10" y1="128" x2="110" y2="128" stroke="#8090b0" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"/><line x1="14" y1="18" x2="106" y2="18" stroke="#8090b0" stroke-width="5" stroke-linecap="round"/><path d="M88 18 C104 62 98 100 70 118" stroke="#ffb020" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" fill="none"/><g stroke="#00e5ff" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" fill="none"><line x1="46" y1="18" x2="52" y2="48"/><line x1="74" y1="18" x2="68" y2="48"/><line x1="60" y1="54" x2="60" y2="88"/><line x1="60" y1="88" x2="54" y2="123"/><line x1="60" y1="88" x2="66" y2="115"/></g><circle cx="60" cy="40" r="7" fill="#00e5ff" stroke="none"/></svg></div><div class="sl-text"><p class="sl-name"><span class="sl-n">Rung 2</span> Feet-assisted hang</p><p><span class="sl-k">What it looks like</span>Toes touching the floor or a box, or one or both feet in a loop band. The bar carries most of your weight and the floor or band takes the rest. Record the assist you used.</p><p><span class="sl-k">Ready for the next rung when</span>You finish every set with only light toe contact or a thinner band, and the hold feels steady.</p></div></li>
<li><div class="sl-fig"><svg viewBox="0 0 120 140" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><rect x="1.5" y="1.5" width="117" height="137" rx="6" fill="#0e1420" stroke="#2a3a54" stroke-width="1.5"/><line x1="10" y1="128" x2="110" y2="128" stroke="#8090b0" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"/><rect x="34" y="116" width="52" height="12" rx="2" fill="none" stroke="#8090b0" stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray="4 3"/><line x1="14" y1="18" x2="106" y2="18" stroke="#8090b0" stroke-width="5" stroke-linecap="round"/><g stroke="#00e5ff" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" fill="none"><line x1="46" y1="18" x2="52" y2="48"/><line x1="74" y1="18" x2="68" y2="48"/><line x1="60" y1="54" x2="60" y2="88"/><line x1="60" y1="88" x2="55" y2="108"/><line x1="60" y1="88" x2="65" y2="108"/></g><circle cx="60" cy="40" r="7" fill="#00e5ff" stroke="none"/></svg></div><div class="sl-text"><p class="sl-name"><span class="sl-n">Rung 3</span> Short controlled holds</p><p><span class="sl-k">What it looks like</span>Feet off the ground, arms straight, for a few seconds at a time. A box or step sits beneath you. Step down under control before your grip gives out.</p><p><span class="sl-k">Ready for the next rung when</span>You finish every set of short holds cleanly and want to lengthen them toward 15 seconds.</p></div></li>
<li><div class="sl-fig"><svg viewBox="0 0 120 140" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><rect x="1.5" y="1.5" width="117" height="137" rx="6" fill="#0e1420" stroke="#2a3a54" stroke-width="1.5"/><line x1="14" y1="18" x2="106" y2="18" stroke="#8090b0" stroke-width="5" stroke-linecap="round"/><g stroke="#00e5ff" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" fill="none"><line x1="46" y1="18" x2="52" y2="48"/><line x1="74" y1="18" x2="68" y2="48"/><line x1="60" y1="54" x2="60" y2="88"/><line x1="60" y1="88" x2="55" y2="108"/><line x1="60" y1="88" x2="65" y2="108"/></g><circle cx="60" cy="40" r="7" fill="#00e5ff" stroke="none"/><circle cx="44" cy="122" r="4" fill="#00e5ff"/><circle cx="60" cy="122" r="4" fill="#00e5ff"/><circle cx="76" cy="122" r="4" fill="#00e5ff"/></svg></div><div class="sl-text"><p class="sl-name"><span class="sl-n">Rung 4</span> Level 1 hang</p><p><span class="sl-k">What it looks like</span>Three sets of 15 seconds, with as much assistance as you need to reach 15. Rest 90 seconds between sets.</p><p><span class="sl-k">Ready for the next rung when</span>You hold 15 seconds across all 3 sets with minimal assistance. Level 2 starts there; see the <a href="/deadhang-progressions/">dead hang progressions</a>.</p></div></li>
